The prompt’s material domain is unbounded: any finite, well-formed sequence of parenthesis groups, not just the example. I’m choosing a single-pass implementation so the proof can use one symbolic scanner invariant over the entire character sequence and avoid a bounded group-size argument. Next I’m mapping the exact fixed-semantics configuration and loop machinery.
